Package: GGMsubho
Type: Package
Title: Sparse Gaussian Graphical Model Estimation with Step-Up Bayesian Horseshoe Selection
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Sagnik", "Bhadury", email = "bhadury@upenn.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Riten", "Mitra", role = "aut"),
    person("Jeremy T.", "Gaskins", role = "aut"))
Description: Estimates sparse networks of conditional dependence from
    high-dimensional continuous data with Graphical-SUBHO (Step-Up Bayesian
    HOrseshoe; Bhadury, Mitra and Gaskins 2023 <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2308.02713>).
    Each variable is regressed on the others under a horseshoe prior (Carvalho,
    Polson and Scott 2010 <doi:10.1093/biomet/asq017>), the predictors are ranked
    by the size of their posterior coefficient, and a Beta-Bernoulli model prior
    and a conjugate working marginal likelihood select one model along the K+1
    nested models. Neighbourhoods are combined by the AND or OR rule of Meinshausen
    and Buhlmann (2006) <doi:10.1214/009053606000000281>, and partial correlations
    are recovered from the coefficients. The regressions run in parallel and their
    results do not depend on the number of cores. The package also provides the
    comparison methods of the article, including the graphical horseshoe, simulators
    with a known graph, accuracy measures, network figures, and a processed gene
    expression panel from triple-negative breast cancer patients in the METABRIC
    study (Curtis et al. 2012 <doi:10.1038/nature10983>).
